```plaintext
1result.sql
```

Reason: All three queries return the same correct rows, but `1result.sql` is the most portable and straightforward:  
• it uses only ANSI‑standard SQL (no dialect‑specific `printf` as in `0result.sql`),  
• avoids unnecessary quoted identifiers (unlike `2result.sql`),  
• and clearly derives the tree count used for ranking while rounding the average income.